  "problems": "The main size guide says for Denim: \"Please see fit and size information on our denim product pages, as they vary by style.\" There is no single denim chart; three product charts recorded (inches only, fractions such as 33 1/2 written as decimals; rows carry an extra \"rise\" field). Even the same style differs by wash (Danielle Lykens vs Montgomery), so a per-product chart is needed for accuracy. None of the charts says whether values are body or garment; basis is inferred. Pants/dresses inches tables also published (e.g. size 0 waist 25.5, low hip 35.75); hip is labelled \"Low Hip\". Pants chart labels size 12 as L while the dresses chart labels it XL."
}